0. DEFINITIONS

   "Licensor" means Gayash Vihangana.

   "Software" means the Mobilux Repair Shop Management System, including its
   source code, database schema, migrations, documentation and any updates the
   Licensor supplies.

   "Licensee" means the business named in the accompanying order, invoice or
   written agreement with the Licensor.

   "Instance" means one running deployment of the Software, serving one
   business, with its own database.

   "Licensee Data" means everything the Licensee and its customers put into an
   Instance: customer records, repair records, bills, payments, uploaded files.


1. GRANT

   On payment in full of the agreed fee, the Licensor grants the Licensee a
   non-exclusive, non-transferable, perpetual licence to install and run one
   Instance of the Software for the Licensee's own repair business, under the
   Licensee's own name and branding.

   This licence covers the Licensee's own employees and contractors while they
   are working for the Licensee.

   Each additional business, brand or trading location requires its own licence
   and its own fee. One licence, one business, one Instance.


2. WHAT THE LICENSEE MAY DO

   a) Run the Instance for its own commercial repair business, without limit on
      the number of repairs, customers, staff accounts or revenue.

   b) Configure the Instance — shop name, logo, contact details, opening hours,
      bank accounts, pricing, discount rules — through the settings provided.

   c) Take and keep its own backups of the Instance and of Licensee Data.

   d) Continue running the Instance indefinitely, whether or not the Licensee
      buys ongoing support. Support and updates are a separate arrangement;
      stopping them does not end this licence.


3. WHAT THE LICENSEE MAY NOT DO

   a) Distribute, publish, sell, rent, lease, sublicense, lend or otherwise make
      the Software available to anyone else, in source or compiled form.

   b) Run the Software, or allow it to be run, for any business other than the
      Licensee's own — including operating it as a service, a hosted product or
      a shared platform for third parties.

   c) Deploy more than one Instance, other than a non-production copy used
      solely for testing or training by the Licensee's own staff.

   d) Remove, obscure or alter any copyright notice or authorship attribution in
      the Software.

   e) Use the Software to build, or assist anyone else in building, a competing
      product.

   The Licensee may modify its own copy of the Software for its own use. Doing so
   ends the Licensor's obligation to support or repair the modified parts, and
   any such modification remains subject to clauses 3(a) to 3(e).


